 Branch mo1306/phase3a-refresh; starting HEAD f236c4a2f94d8cd8e763aaa4bd6c52d703429692. Main and other worktrees remained read-only. [task-context.json](C:/Users/melsa/Documents/Codex/cca-mo1306-3a-refresh/repositories/cca-conformance/evidence/mo1306/phase3a-environment-capture/task-context.json)"},{"name":"C3CB","number":2,"result":"Production authority 701d48ee2012675966360dda775ab13013c09ab9. Installed core/publication/filesystem/helper bytes exactly match that commit. [source-handle-audit.json](C:/Users/melsa/Documents/Codex/cca-mo1306-3a-refresh/repositories/cca-conformance/evidence/mo1306/phase3a-environment-capture/source-handle-audit.json)"},{"name":"Historical failure preservation","number":3,"result":"Original run e89b8e91-c3c5-402d-9e6f-000bd2a102ba, blocked receipts, accepted eight native groups, and three prior faithful reproductions retained unchanged. Original acquisition INPUT_ERROR / exit 11 became publication ARTIFACT_ERROR / exit 17, leaving evidence/result only. No prior disposition rewritten. [preservation-audit.json](C:/Users/melsa/Documents/Codex/cca-mo1306-3a-refresh/repositories/cca-conformance/evidence/mo1306/phase3a-environment-capture/preservation-audit.json)"},{"name":"Frozen four-file contract","number":4,"result":"Frozen operational-input-error success requires result, evidence, artifacts manifest and completion marker: exact four files with valid identities/digests/run-id. Publication failure may override the input error. The three prior faithful passes remain separate evidence. [methodology-audit.json](C:/Users/melsa/Documents/Codex/cca-mo1306-3a-refresh/repositories/cca-conformance/evidence/mo1306/phase3a-environment-capture/methodology-audit.json)"},{"name":"Manifest finalization source site","number":5,"result":"C3CB src/core.mjs -> publication.mjs publish -> filesystem.mjs checkPaths -> target absence check -> fs.renameSync. Original source: C:\\Users\\melsa\\Documents\\Codex\\cca-mo1306-3a-refresh\\.cache\\mo1306-phase3a-final\\n-20260927T120240-b3df86\\error-input\\.memoryos-ci\\out\\e89b8e91-c3c5-402d-9e6f-000bd2a102ba\\.pending\\memoryos-ci-artifacts.json; destination: C:\\Users\\melsa\\Documents\\Codex\\cca-mo1306-3a-refresh\\.cache\\mo1306-phase3a-final\\n-20260927T120240-b3df86\\error-input\\.memoryos-ci\\out\\e89b8e91-c3c5-402d-9e6f-000bd2a102ba\\memoryos-ci-artifacts.json; parent: C:\\Users\\melsa\\Documents\\Codex\\cca-mo1306-3a-refresh\\.cache\\mo1306-phase3a-final\\n-20260927T120240-b3df86\\error-input\\.memoryos-ci\\out\\e89b8e91-c3c5-402d-9e6f-000bd2a102ba. Exact original failing API remains unrecorded: pre-rename check is an ordinal/source-order hypothesis. [Node binding](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nodejs/node/v24.21.0/src/node_file.cc) reaches bundled [libuv MoveFileExW with MOVEFILE_REPLACE_EXISTING](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nodejs/node/v24.21.0/deps/uv/src/win/fs.c)."},{"name":"Pre-rename helper role","number":6,"result":"Fixed Windows PowerShell child checks path ancestors, NTFS and reparse metadata using DriveInfo/GetAttributes. No explicit manifest FileStream; stdin/stdout are pipes. Successful check resolves only after child close and unchanged deadline checks. [Node close/exit semantics](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nodejs/node/v24.21.0/doc/api/child_process.md). .NET [reference source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/microsoft/referencesource/main/mscorlib/system/io/file.cs) can use transient metadata/search handles; it is not installed-CLR binary proof."},{"name":"Observation architecture","number":7,"result":"Plan preceded execution. Engineering-only Node builtin observer plus native QPC process query/signal sampler, shared ReadDirectoryChangesW subscription, bounded directory/SDDL snapshots, descriptor ledger and post-run event queries. No production edit, injected lock/delay or security change. [observation-plan.json](C:/Users/melsa/Documents/Codex/cca-mo1306-3a-refresh/repositories/cca-conformance/evidence/mo1306/phase3a-environment-capture/observation-plan.json)"},{"name":"Observation precision","number":8,"result":"Common QPC basis, frequency 10000000Hz and resolution 100.0ns; 393 process samples, achieved maximum gap 47.2826ms (20ms target). [Pinned libuv QPC conversion](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nodejs/node/v24.21.0/deps/uv/src/win/util.c) and [CPython3.12.14 conversion](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/v3.12.14/Python/pytime.c) use the same counter without process offsets; conversion rounding and [cross-thread +/-1 tick ambiguity](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/sysinfo/acquiring-high-resolution-time-stamps) remain. UTC is correlation only; polling never supplies exact kernel exit."},{"name":"Process timeline","number":9,"result":"One new run, root PID 9448, helper 18 PID 10148/parent 9448. Node-relative monotonic ms (paired QPC brackets): spawn9398.2309, request9451.0005, response9924.2124, exit9959.7871, close9959.8530; close1438.2982ms before unchanged helper deadline. External process-signaled interval is QPC[39097390082500,39097421035700]ns; it bounds observation, not exact kernel exit, and its upper bound may lag Node close/rename. All 20 helpers completed; 41 process identities include root/helpers/consoles. No owned processes remain. Relative to common capture QPC start, helper signal bounds are 10863.6491\u201310894.6023ms and parent signal bounds 12252.3345\u201312284.5087ms. The separate topology trace last includes helper 18 at its 10775ms snapshot and excludes it at10885ms; root last appears at12218ms and final cleanup is empty by12331ms. That trace lacks its exact QPC epoch and individual enumeration durations, so these topology anchors are not shifted into the common timeline or asserted as exact disappearance times. [capture-summary.json](C:/Users/melsa/Documents/Codex/cca-mo1306-3a-refresh/repositories/cca-conformance/evidence/mo1306/phase3a-environment-capture/capture-summary.json)"},{"name":"File-I/O timeline","number":10,"result":"Manifest rename API starts at Node-relative9960.4529ms and returns successfully at9961.9369ms; completion write bracket11330.3051\u201311331.1822ms; product import settles at11332.1268ms with exit 11. Temporary manifest write has common observer-relative brackets9220.9941\u20139220.9945ms before and9222.6557\u20139222.6566ms after; parent import settles at12245.5196\u201312245.5210ms. Pending manifest creation precedes helper 18; evidence/result already finalized; pending directory removed before completion. 29 notification batches and 8 directory snapshots independently record ordered create/rename/remove/marker changes; delivery timestamps are not kernel mutation times. [capture-summary.json](C:/Users/melsa/Documents/Codex/cca-mo1306-3a-refresh/repositories/cca-conformance/evidence/mo1306/phase3a-environment-capture/capture-summary.json)"},{"name":"Actual OS/Node error if captured","number":11,"result":"No new publication Node/Windows error occurred. Expected acquisition error was ENOENT, errno -4058, syscall lstat, path ending error-input/missing.mip, dest null; mapped diagnostic MO1306_INPUT_READ/ACQUISITION and final exit 11. Original publication code/errno/syscall/path/destination and underlying helper error remain uncaptured. No raw Win32 error inferred from ARTIFACT_WRITE. [capture-summary.json](C:/Users/melsa/Documents/Codex/cca-mo1306-3a-refresh/repositories/cca-conformance/evidence/mo1306/phase3a-environment-capture/capture-summary.json)"},{"name":"Handle/lock evidence","number":12,"result":"No relevant retained-file-handle race or external lock proven. Source closes product read/write descriptors; final descriptor ledger empty. Process handle counts and shared watch are indirect evidence only. [ExitProcess](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/processthreadsapi/nf-processthreadsapi-exitprocess) closes exiting-process object handles before signaling; observers may retain process objects and other processes may retain their own duplicated handles. No exhaustive global handle inventory. [source-handle-audit.json](C:/Users/melsa/Documents/Codex/cca-mo1306-3a-refresh/repositories/cca-conformance/evidence/mo1306/phase3a-environment-capture/source-handle-audit.json)"},{"name":"Directory state","number":13,"result":"New snapshots retain existence, names/types/sizes, path lengths, attributes and reparse state around manifest notifications. ACL/SDDL was queried only before/after capture, not within the critical rename window. Final run has exact four regular files; pending absent, manifest 381 bytes and marker 188 bytes; relevant observed paths non-reparse and not read-only. These new-run snapshots do not reconstruct original conditions. [runs/20260927T212537-f27c81/summary.json](C:/Users/melsa/Documents/Codex/cca-mo1306-3a-refresh/repositories/cca-conformance/evidence/mo1306/phase3a-environment-capture/runs/20260927T212537-f27c81/summary.json)"},{"name":"Windows event evidence","number":14,"result":"Capture21:25:38.062647\u201321:25:50.548585UTC queried with 10-second margins. System all levels, Application error/warning, Defender, Kernel-Power/Thermal and CodeIntegrity metadata were readable and bounded queries found no matching records, without truncation. Security metadata access was denied; its bounded ID query returned NoMatchingEvents, retained without claiming Security availability/completeness. Absence does not prove no interference or interruption. [windows-eventlog.json](C:/Users/melsa/Documents/Codex/cca-mo1306-3a-refresh/repositories/cca-conformance/evidence/mo1306/phase3a-environment-capture/windows-eventlog.json)"},{"name":"Security-software evidence","number":15,"result":"No explicit correlated Defender/security event or attributed file operation was found. Antivirus is not blamed, disabled or reconfigured. No security-software cause established."},{"name":"New observed run 1","number":16,"result":"One new genuine run: 20260927T212537-f27c81; run-id97226496-a9f2-4846-a293-5878d2c56b79. INPUT_ERROR / exit 11, COMPLETE, exact four-file bundle; 20 helpers; no observer errors or remaining owned PIDs. 94 installed members unchanged. [runs/20260927T212537-f27c81/summary.json](C:/Users/melsa/Documents/Codex/cca-mo1306-3a-refresh/repositories/cca-conformance/evidence/mo1306/phase3a-environment-capture/runs/20260927T212537-f27c81/summary.json)"},{"name":"New observed run 2 if used","number":17,"result":"NOT USED. Successful repetition alone would not supply the missing historical attribution or methodology exception."},{"name":"New observed run 3 if used","number":18,"result":"NOT USED. New genuine product execution count remains 1 of maximum 3."},{"name":"Hypothesis witness if used","number":19,"result":"NOT USED. No independently supported concrete historical mechanism justified an injected engineering witness."},{"name":"Root-cause classification","number":20,"result":"UNRESOLVED. No permitted proven-cause category supported. HISTORICAL_CAUSE_UNRECOVERABLE_CURRENT_BEHAVIOR_STABLE is not permitted: section20 criterion10 methodology permission NOT_ESTABLISHED; criterion2 historical error nonrecoverability only PARTIALLY_ESTABLISHED. New successful observation does not override either requirement. [section20-assessment.json](C:/Users/melsa/Documents/Codex/cca-mo1306-3a-refresh/repositories/cca-conformance/evidence/mo1306/phase3a-environment-capture/section20-assessment.json)"},{"name":"Product defect disposition","number":21,"result":"No deterministic product defect proven; no production correction attempted. Historical failure remains valid and unresolved."},{"name":"Harness defect disposition","number":22,"result":"No historical harness defect proven. New observer setup corrections were made before product execution and bounded microchecks passed (notification decoding and unsigned Windows path-result typing); the initial preservation-dictionary comparison was also corrected before execution. These do not explain the old failure. [observer-microcheck.json](C:/Users/m